// scrml.dev /reference/errors/W-PROGRAM-001
//
// Reference page for W-PROGRAM-001. No `<program>` root element found.
//
// SPEC anchors: §4.12.2, §4.12.8, §4.12.9, §34.
//
// Written 2026-07-26. Prose derived from the compiler's own emission message in
// compiler/src; the reproducer below is the exact source compiled against the
// linked compiler to verify what this code does.

<page>

    // REFERENCE SIDEBAR opt-in — static, page-scoped, zero JS. The nav is
    // authored once in app.scrml and hidden by default; this shows it and
    // marks THIS page's link active. See scripts/gen-reference-nav.mjs.
    #{
        /* !important is load-order, not laziness: the shell's app.css is linked
           AFTER this page's stylesheet, so its `.refnav{display:none}` default
           wins at equal specificity. */
        .ref-shell { display: grid !important; }
        .refnav { display: block !important; }
        .refnav-link[data-ref="errors/W-PROGRAM-001"] {
            color: rgb(125 211 252);
            background-color: rgb(14 165 233 / 0.10);
            border-left-color: rgb(56 189 248);
            font-weight: 600;
        }
    }

    <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-3xl">

        <header class="not-prose mb-8 pb-6 border-b border-slate-200">
            <div class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-500 mb-2">
                Reference &rsaquo; Errors
            </div>
            <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-amber-700 font-mono">
                W-PROGRAM-001
            </h1>
            <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 mt-2">
                No <code>&lt;program&gt;</code> root element found.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-4 text-xs">
                <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-amber-50 text-amber-700 rounded font-semibold">
                    Warning
                </span>
                <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 rounded">
                    Compile-time
                </span>
                <a href="https://github.com/bryanmaclee/scrml/blob/main/compiler/SPEC.md#4"
                   class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 underline">
                    SPEC §4.12.2 (normative)
                </a>
            </div>
        </header>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
            What it means
        </h2>

        <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
            <code>&lt;program&gt;</code> is where a file declares database connections, protection settings and HTML spec version. A file with none still compiles — the defaults apply — but has no place to put that configuration, so the compiler nudges. Two shapes are recognised and stay silent: a <strong>pure module file</strong> (no markup nodes at all) and a <strong>non-entry page file</strong> (declares a <code>&lt;page&gt;</code> at file scope), because in a multi-page app the <code>&lt;program&gt;</code> is declared once in the entry file.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
            Minimal reproducer
        </h2>

        <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            This is the exact source compiled against the linked compiler and verified to produce <code>W-PROGRAM-001</code>.
        </p>

        <pre class="bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-md text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>&lt;h1&gt;no program root&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;plain markup only&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
            How to fix
        </h2>

        <ol class="space-y-3 text-slate-700 list-decimal list-outside ml-6">
            <li>
                <strong>Wrap the content in <code>&lt;program&gt;</code>.</strong>
                Correct for an entry file that needs configuration.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Ignore it for a page or module file.</strong>
                If the file declares a <code>&lt;page&gt;</code> or contains no markup, this lint should not be firing — see the suppression rules above.
            </li>
        </ol>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
            Related
        </h2>

        <ul class="space-y-1 text-slate-700">
            <li>
                <a href="/reference/elements/program" class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 underline">&lt;program&gt;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="/reference/elements/page" class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 underline">&lt;page&gt;</a>
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
            Specification
        </h2>

        <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
            Normative text: <strong>§4.12.2, §4.12.8, §4.12.9, §34</strong>. Spec lives at
            <a href="https://github.com/bryanmaclee/scrml/blob/main/compiler/SPEC.md"
               class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 underline">
                compiler/SPEC.md
            </a>.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-10 text-sm">
            <a href="/reference" class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 underline">
                &larr; Reference
            </a>
        </p>

    </article>

</>
